{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Teddy has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rectangular blocks each of which measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c18d02ad0faaf33629223dfae43e0c8fb1ba6062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/b/a6bc2ae4b358f0d6e27b163a7b1beae3c30f0c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35df5f1800eac426739f20cae1ff726bc9fbedf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. He builds a stack that is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c37b9559e0be9bb6b0da86170ea69d8d7c7667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> high, where each block can be stacked on any of its faces. What is the smallest number of blocks that Teddy could use to make this stack?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4614bccaf693001db67d6f5de0f86dbe090b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~4\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~6\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~7\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This question in easier words is just: \"What's the least amount of numbers from {<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/774055f560b65f00f2976674966367dca4327f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />} that are required to give a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\"\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/45840ce5bed80df0c3b25afe359514c881827952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) }\\ 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"30\" /> since we need four <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s and one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~any1sgame\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018031828\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.008 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 53/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\n